.TH mnnn-tui 1  "mnnn-tui 2.1.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-tui \- Launch the terminal UI
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn tui\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch the terminal UI
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Everything you can act on is clickable: menus, tiles, sidebar, popup rows, form fields, import picker entries and the key buttons ([X] closes any popup).
.PP
Import (i): pick a file or a whole folder (A imports the folder, recursing). If a symbol cannot be guessed from a file name, a popup asks for it, showing the file name on its own line, its folder below and (file i of n) during folder imports. After an import, if no tile shows data yet, the focused tile loads the first imported series.
.PP
Help (? or F1): follow links with Tab and Enter or a click, Backspace goes back, / searches from any topic; a clickable key bar at the bottom lists the shortcuts.
.PP
Tiles: Tab / Shift\-Tab focus the next / previous tile, Alt\-1..9 jumps to tile [n]; the status line shows these keys.
.PP
Ranges: [ and ] (or a click on a date) open a date and time picker for a chart's period or a list tile's range (from / to; \e clears it); arrows or digits set year, month, day, hour and minute. T (Data > Filters > Time range...) sets one time range for every view and tile, from then to; x leaves an end open.
.PP
Symbols: the sidebar symbol filter (m, Data > Filters > Symbol) lists only the chosen symbols; search ignores separators (btc\-usdt finds BTC/USDT) and word order.
.PP
Loading: series load in the background; a tile shows a progress bar (bars read of the total) or a spinner while the total is unknown, and the UI stays responsive.
.PP
History (Y, View > History): a collapsible bar on the left shows every action as a tree, forks indented; u / U step back / forward and restore the filters, time range and theme, Enter or a click on a row goes to that action. Authors (A, File > Authors...): add, edit, delete and pick the current author that new actions are attributed to.
.PP
Projects menu (Alt\-P): Projects... (P) lists projects and their live searches, results and journals; Live searches... (F) and Save search as live search... (B) keep a sidebar search that always runs on current data; Journals... (J) holds entries in Markdown or LaTeX with images, notes and highlights on selected words (v selects, m highlights, n notes). In the sidebar, a adds the selected series to a project.
.PP
See mnnn help tui, mnnn help import, mnnn help history, mnnn help authors, mnnn help projects, mnnn help live\-searches, mnnn help journals and mnnn help help.
